# Plan: Unit Test Suite Complete Refactoring

## User decisions (confirmed via questions)
- FULL scope: restructure existing tests AND write new tests for every logic file (internal/ + app/gui pure-logic)
- Gio-heavy app/gui files (~41): document in todo/test_observations.md as unit-untestable; integration suite covers them
- Single assert.Equal on whole struct/slice = one assert; require.* preconditions allowed in Arrange
- Table-driven tests ALLOWED with named t.Run subtests (subtest names follow When{Scenario}_{Behavior})
- Phased by package, each phase independently verifiable (coverage gate + commit)

## Target structure rules (from user requirements)
- Mirror impl path: `internal/services/settingsFileLoader.go` → `test/unit/internal/services/settingsFileLoader/{funcName}_test.go`
- One folder per impl file; one _test.go per public function/method (lowerCamel: `loadSettingsFile_test.go`)
- Package per folder: `{implFileName}_test` (Go: one package per dir)
- Test names: `Test{Scenario}_{ExpectedBehavior}` — deepest relevant condition in scenario
- AAA comments: // Arrange, // Act, // Assert (pre-act guard asserts OK in Arrange)
- One logical assert per test (whole-struct equality counts as one)
- testify only (assert/require/mock); gofakeit for fuzzing wherever possible
- NO tests for: pure data structs, internal/registry/, *_testexports.go (integration_test tag) — must never be imported by unit tests
- Private code tested only via public entry points; NO test-only helpers added to implementation
- Unreachable code → document in todo/test_observations.md (do NOT modify impl)

